POE2TRADE.MODS SUBMODULE – README

OVERVIEW
The poe2trade.mods submodule provides functionalities to scrape and update mod data for the Path of Exile (PoE) trading system. It uses browser automation (with Selenium and PyAutoGUI) to interact with the PoE trade website and extract mod filter options, then processes this data to match known mod patterns. The submodule offers a command-line interface to run the scraping and updating workflows independently or together.

FILE DESCRIPTIONS
main.py

Serves as the entry point for the mods submodule.

Reads command-line arguments; if none are provided, defaults to both ‘scrape’ and ‘update’.

Calls the corresponding functions: it runs scrape_mods if the argument ‘scrape’ is present, and update_mods if the argument ‘update’ is present.

scrape_mods.py

Automates the process of scraping mod filter data from the PoE trade website.

Uses PyAutoGUI to launch Chrome in remote debugging mode and Selenium to attach to the browser.

Navigates to the trade page, ensures that the filters are visible and toggled on, then collects all <li> elements with class “multiselect__element.”

Applies additional transformations on the scraped data (e.g., grouping, renaming, filtering, and reassigning group numbers) and exports the result to an Excel file (mods_trade.xlsx) in the submodule’s files folder.

Finally, forcefully terminates the Chrome processes.

update_mods.py

Processes the Excel file generated by the scraping process (mods_trade.xlsx).

Filters the data to keep rows with “Stat Filters” in the GroupName column, renames OptionText to Mod, and drops unnecessary columns.

For each row, compares the mod text against unique mod lists for different item types (body armour, amulet, ring, belt) using the compare_mods function from poe2trade.utils.mods_utils; flags are set accordingly.

Builds two additional sheets: one for Corruption mods (listing each corruption mod) and one for Rune mods (listing details like RuneName, MartialWeaponMod, and ArmourMod).

Writes all three sheets (“Main”, “Corruption”, “Rune”) to an updated Excel file (mods_trade_updated.xlsx).

WORKFLOW
Scraping:

Run the mods submodule with the “scrape” argument (e.g., “python -m poe2trade.mods scrape”) to launch the browser automation workflow.

This process will navigate to the PoE trade site, toggle filters, scrape mod options, and export the data to an Excel file.

Updating:

Run the mods submodule with the “update” argument (e.g., “python -m poe2trade.mods update”) to process the scraped data.

The update workflow cleans, categorizes, and matches mod texts with known patterns and produces an updated Excel file with additional sheets for Corruption and Rune data.

DEPENDENCIES
Selenium: For browser automation and interacting with the PoE trade website.

PyAutoGUI: For automating keyboard and mouse actions (launching Chrome in debug mode).

Pandas: For data manipulation and exporting data to Excel files.

The submodule also relies on internal modules (e.g., poe2trade.utils.mods_utils) and paths defined in poe2trade.

CONTRIBUTIONS
Follow the established structure and coding style as seen in the other submodules.

Ensure new functionality maintains separation between scraping and updating workflows.

Test changes using the provided command-line interface in main.py.

